# Allowlist. This folder can also be a live install, sitting next to private
# notes, logs, spooled hook payloads and evidence files. Ignore everything and
# opt files in one at a time, so nothing private gets swept into a commit.
*

!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.env.example
!README.md
!requirements.txt
!docker-compose.yml

!agent_memory.py
!agent_memory_hook.py
!agent_identity.py
!identity_history.py
!codex_transcript_import.py
!start.py
!test_agent_identity.py
!test_identity_postgres.py

!docs/
!docs/*.md
!hooks/
!hooks/*.example.json
!schema/
!schema/*.sql
!skills/
!skills/agent-memory-blueprint/
!skills/agent-memory-blueprint/SKILL.md

# Belt and braces: never these, even if someone adds an allow rule above.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.jsonl
*.zlib
*.dump
*.sql.gz
